  "adaptations": "Set DEVICES to one CPU-NUMA device per socket, TENSOR_SPLIT to an equal weight per device, and THREADS to physical cores per socket minus one, leaving a core for that device's dispatcher. The defaults describe a dual-socket ten-core host. GGML_CPU_NUMA_THREADS follows THREADS; the four-socket profiles hard-code 15 and must not be copied to a smaller machine. Speculative decoding needs the MTP sidecar as its own file: add --spec-type draft-mtp, --spec-draft-model, --spec-draft-device with the same device list, --spec-draft-ngl all and --spec-draft-n-max 2 (depth 3 measured 4 percent slower). Do not launch under a restrictive taskset: a restricted mask yields one worker per socket. The published engine also needs patches/glm5next-x16-moe-expert-bound.patch or the first token aborts. No LD_LIBRARY_PATH is set: a self-built engine finds its own libraries through the rpath cmake writes into build/bin. The four-socket profiles point it at separately rebuilt private libraries, which do not exist in a fresh reconstruction."
